OUGHOUT MARCH AND EARLY APRIL.'}{'symbol': 'NLSN', 'date': '2021-03-19 12:59:00', 'title': 'WOMEN 50+ ARE UNDERREPRESENTED ON TOP TV PROGRAMS', 'text': 'NEW YORK, MARCH 19, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0TO COMMEMORATE WOMEN\'S HISTORY MONTH, NIELSEN (NYSE: NLSN) TODAY RELEASED "SHATTERING STEREOTYPES: HOW TODAY\'S WOMEN OVER 50 ARE REDEFINING WHAT\'S POSSIBLE ON-SCREEN, AT WORK AND AT HOME", PART OF THE NIELSEN DIVERSE INTELLIGENCE SERIES. USING CUSTOM ANALYSIS FROM THE RECENTLY-LAUNCHED GRACENOTE INCLUSION ANALYTICS, THE REPORT UNCOVERS THAT WOMEN OVER THE AGE OF 50 ARE UNDERREPRESENTED ON TOP TV PROGRAMS AND WHEN THEY ARE SEEN, THEY OFTEN PLAY STEREOTYPICAL ROLES.'}{'symbol': 'PENN', 'date': '2021-03-19 16:20:00', 'title': 'PENN NATIONAL GAMING LAUNCHES DIVERSITY SCHOLARSHIP PROGRAM FOR CHILDREN OF TEAM MEMBERS', 'text': "WYOMISSING, PA.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--PENN NATIONAL GAMING, INC. (NASDAQ: PENN)(“PENN NATIONAL” OR THE “COMPANY”) ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT IT HAS LAUNCHED A NEW DIVERSITY SCHOLARSHIP PROGRAM FOR THE CHILDREN OF ITS TEAM MEMBERS, WHICH REFLECTS THE COMPANY'S COMMITMENT TO EQUITY IN POST-SECONDARY EDUCATION OPPORTUNITIES FOR STUDENTS. PENN NATIONAL IS PARTNERING WITH THE PUBLIC EDUCATION FOUNDATION (“PEF”) TO ADMINISTER THE DIVERSITY SCHOLARSHIP PROGRAM AND HAS COMMITTED $1 MILLION ANNUALLY TO FUND THE P"}{'symbol': 'PNC', 'date': '2021-03-19 08:47:00', 'title': 'PNC ANNOUNCES REDEMPTION OF 2.150 PERCENT SENIOR BANK NOTES DUE APRIL 29, 2021', 'text': 'PITTSBURGH, MARCH 19, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- THE PNC FINANCIAL SERVICES GROUP, INC. (NYSE: PNC) TODAY ANNOUNCED THE REDEMPTION ON MARCH 30, 2021, OF ALL OF THE OUTSTANDING SENIOR NOTES DUE APRIL 29, 2021, ISSUED BY PNC BANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION IN THE AMOUNT OF $1,250,000,000 (CUSIP 69353REW4). THE SECURITIES HAVE A DISTRIBUTION RATE OF 2.150 PERCENT AND AN ORIGINAL SCHEDULED MATURITY DATE OF APRIL 29, 2021.'}{'symbol': 'ROP', 'date': '2021-03-19 16:15:00', 'title': 'ROPER TECHNOLOGIES ANNOUNCES DIVIDEND', 'text': '